{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "New Interests and Aspirations"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Restaurant Management Certificate"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le04ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Future Time Clauses,  As Soon As, Until"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use time clauses to give information about time and sequence in future actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>, <span class=\"italic\">If</span>, <span class=\"italic\">When</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> Before and After </span>in time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Future time clauses explain what needs to happen or which condition needs to be satisfied before a future event can occur."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional with these time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br/> <ul>As soon as/Until/When/Before/After + Subject + Simple Present tense, Subject + will/be going to + Simple Present tense"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">As soon as</span> means almost at the same time. An action in the future will occur immediately after the action introduced by the time clause finishes. <br/> </br>Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul>As soon as I register, I will know for sure.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Until</span> means for the duration of an action. The action introduced by the time clause will lead to another action once it is completed. You normally use <span class=\"italic\">until </span>after the main clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">I'll keep coming to this class <span class=\"strong\">until </span>I hear from the registrar's office. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Before </span>means at an earlier time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">After </span>means at a later time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> means on the condition that ..."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When </span>means at the time of doing something."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">After </span>I register at the college, I'll have a look at the syllabus for each course."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Oh and before I forget, I will be working at the restaurant <span class=\"strong\">until </span>it closes when you visit this weekend. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> If </span>summer ever arrives, I'll be sailing a lot. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Future Continuous for Interrupted Action "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future. The action in the future is often interrupted by another action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment. When you use the Future Continuous, a future action can also be interrupted by another one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><span class=\"italic\">I'll be taking five courses when my mom comes to visit.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The ongoing action (taking five courses) is going to be interrupted the mom's visit."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two ways to use the Future Continuous tense: <ul> <li>You use the Future Continuous to indicate that a longer action in the future will be interrupted by a shorter action in the future. </li></ul>Structure: will + be + present participle of the verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I will be working at the restaurant when you visit.</span><ul> <li>You use the Future Continuous to express the idea that two actions will be happening at the same time. The actions are parallel. You use two Future Continuous actions in the same sentence.</li></ul> <br/> Structure:</br><ul> am/is/are + going to be + present participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">m going to be working </span>and studying when you'<span class=\"strong\">re going to be killing </span>time playing computer games.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'm going to be working when you are there. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be studying, attending class and working when you are killing time. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I will be working at the restaurant. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'll be taking five courses and working when my mom comes to visit."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "syllabus "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(a \u200bplan \u200bshowing) the \u200bsubjects or \u200bbooks to be \u200bstudied in a \u200bparticular \u200bcourse, \u200bespecially a \u200bcourse that \u200bleads to an \u200bexam"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'll have a look at the syllabus for each course. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about education and school."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "textbook"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bbook that \u200bcontains \u200bdetailed \u200binformation about a \u200bsubject for \u200bpeople who are \u200bstudying that \u200bsubject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am going to have to buy all the textbooks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to register"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put \u200binformation, \u200bespecially \u200byour \u200bname, into an \u200bofficial \u200blist or \u200brecord"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  As soon as I register, I will know my schedule. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "elective"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a \u200bsubject that someone can \u200bchoose to \u200bstudy as \u200bpart of a \u200bcourse"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:It looks like I will take three core courses and one or two electives."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lecture hall"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large room with tiered or auditorium-style seating, or a building, used for holding lectures"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Business Communications course will be at the lecture hall in Boston on Tuesday evenings. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to kill time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to do something that is not important, while waiting for time to pass"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll be studying, attending class and working when you are killing time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have one's nose in a book"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be reading or studying from books all the time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's too bad you won't have time because you'll have your nose in your books."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to crew"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to work as a team on a boat to keep it running properly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's too bad you won't have time to crew on the boat with me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to run around like a headless chicken"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to run about in a frenzied manner, distractedly, crazily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I guess we'll both be running around like headless chickens. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob06aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research an English college or university for a course you would like to take."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes about the course including a description and the requirements to get into the course."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell a friend about the course and explain why you want to take it."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about education."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes about a course. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about education"}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hey V, that's fantastic news! Sounds like the life-coaching was great. What's next?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: After I register at the college, I'll have a look at the syllabus for each course. I am going to have to buy all the textbooks. I'll be taking five courses and working when my mom comes to visit. I won't have much time for her.", "id": 1}, {"time": "20000", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: When I have free time, I will take her out for lunch or to the museum. What are the courses you'll be taking?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: As soon as I register, I will know for sure. It looks like I will take Management of Food Operations, Restaurant Costs and Control, Business Communications and one or two electives.", "id": 2}, {"time": "40000", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Sounds great. And where are the classes going to be held. Are they all at the college?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Mostly, but I think the Business Communications course will be at the lecture hall in Boston on Tuesday evenings.", "id": 3}, {"time": "53500", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm going to be working when you are there. Otherwise I would drive you back.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That's kind of you Peter. Oh and before I forget, I will be working at the restaurant until it closes when you visit this weekend. I won't have more than an hour to see you. I don't expect we'll be seeing as much of each other, unfortunately. I'll be studying, attending class and working when you are killing time. So while I am working at home you can't come over. I will need to concentrate .", "id": 4}, {"time": "83000", "image": "engenn10le04ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:I get it. If summer ever arrives, I'll be sailing a lot. It's too bad you won't have time to crew with me. You'll have your nose in your books.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I guess we'll both be running around like headless chickens. Before we get so busy, don't forget we're having dinner at the restaurant tomorrow night!", "id": 5}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le04ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le04ob06re2img05.jpg"}}], "id": 1}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about education and character traits. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss plans, hopes and expectations for the future."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Would you return to school in the future to continue studying? If so, what would you study?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you like being very busy? Why? Why not? "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can talk about what I will be doing or what I'm going to do. "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Let's go back to school study something new!"}], "id": 0}, {"type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nVanessa tells Peter about her new plan.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_a